# Security Policy

## Reporting Security Issues

If you discover a security vulnerability in this portfolio website, please report it responsibly:

**Email:** tvaidya@mun.ca
**Subject:** Security Vulnerability Report - Portfolio Website

Please include:
- Description of the vulnerability
- Steps to reproduce
- Potential impact
- Suggested fix (if any)

## Response Timeline

- **Acknowledgment:** Within 48 hours
- **Initial Assessment:** Within 5 business days
- **Resolution Target:** Within 30 days for confirmed vulnerabilities

## Scope

This policy applies to:
- https://www.tvaidya.top/
- All subdomains and paths

## Out of Scope

- Third-party services (EmailJS, GitHub, LinkedIn)
- Social engineering attacks
- Physical security
- Issues requiring user interaction beyond normal browsing

## Safe Harbor

We support safe harbor for security researchers who:
- Make a good faith effort to avoid privacy violations
- Do not destroy or degrade data
- Do not disrupt services
- Report findings promptly
- Allow reasonable time for remediation before disclosure

## Recognition

Security researchers who report valid vulnerabilities will be acknowledged (with permission) in our security advisories.

